    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter today\u2019s slate with a potent core, anchored by **Yordan Alvarez** (78.25) and **Trea Turner** (77.18), both of whom are projected as our strongest plays. **Yordan Alvarez** benefits from an elite xwOBA profile and a highly favorable matchup against Chandler, while **Trea Turner**\u2014our primary engine for SB scarcity\u2014gets a significant boost from a generous 4.75 xERA opposing starter in V\u00e1squez. **Kyle Schwarber** (76.47) rounds out the tier of elite starts, leveraging his leadoff position and strong power profile in the same matchup against V\u00e1squez. Meanwhile, **Junior Caminero** (65.10) provides a sturdy floor despite a slight park penalty, as his batting order position remains a vital catalyst for run production.\n\nTactically, the benching of **Carson Benge** (42.20) was the most difficult decision, as he narrowly missed the cut due to the sheer difficulty of facing Logan Gilbert. The optimizer prioritized the consistency of **Jose Fernandez** (56.27) and **Caleb Durbin** (56.67), the latter of whom is a critical start today; despite hitting ninth, **Caleb Durbin** is a \"must-play\" due to his elite speed and the 90% steal-rate opportunity presented by the slow delivery of Baz. We are monitoring **Luke Raley** (46.55) closely, as his pending lineup status creates a minor volatility risk, and **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (50.71) faces a stiff defensive challenge against a high-velocity catcher and a difficult platoon matchup against Jump. Outside of those factors, the Zebras are well-positioned, provided **Christian Yelich** (54.28) can overcome the hurdle of a sub-3.00 xERA from McDonald to maintain his efficiency.",
